3. Defect found at the source: the render was not reproducible
   First receipt run: FPR-CHECK VERDICT FAIL, both halves "not this derivation".
   Two renders of the SAME fixtures carried different tx digests:
     run A  0ffc1013... / d38c729c...      run B  8e12184b... / be7eb5eb...
   Cause: ledger._write_tx does `ts = ts_utc or now_utc()` and compute_tx_id
   hashes that ts. The producer only stamped apimarket._now_utc, so ledger
   filled the tx ts from the wall clock; two renders inside one second agreed
   (measured: html equal True), renders seconds apart did not.
   Fix, producer only: preview_R2119.py stamps apimarket._now_utc AND
   ledger.now_utc from the same fixture list and restores both.
   After the fix, two separate processes three seconds apart:
     html equal True 21556B sha256 afb57721c7420fc7
     json equal True 34641B

